{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"agent_message","text":"The first judge pilot is fully parseable but scientifically inadequate: it chooses A 50–100% of the time by condition and agrees on the same underlying story in only 9/22 pairs. Raw order-level accuracy is therefore not interpretable. I’m retaining this negative evaluator result, strengthening the symmetric rubric, and rerunning Qwen with its reasoning mode enabled before deciding whether the anchor is genuinely at floor."}}
