{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_136","type":"agent_message","text":"The main result is now clear. The unconstrained anchor replicates leakage (mean mapped score +16.3, 95% bootstrap CI +4.7 to +29.1; permutation p=.020), but once a neutral story brief fixes content, the no-outline condition is already at floor (−0.15, CI −2.87 to +2.40). The outline is not distinguishable from no outline or irrelevant context. Decoys invert the signal. Projection removal creates a dramatic inverted score, but it also collapses stories to a mean 102 words versus 488 for random removal, so it is not evidence of selective causal removal."}}
